  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Huntington Ingalls has $2.9B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date across 64 awards, with an average award size of $45.9M. Obligations are down 29.9% year over year. Ship Building and Repairing is the dominant market for Huntington Ingalls with $2.8B in obligations this fiscal year to date. Engineering Services accounts for $58.4M and Other Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance accounts for $39.6M. Historical obligations show Huntington Ingalls peaked at $4.2B in FY25 and then moved to $2.9B in FY26. Ship Building and Repairing makes up the vast majority of current-year obligations for Huntington Ingalls, while the remaining listed NAICS categories represent comparatively small shares. Award activity for Huntington Ingalls this fiscal year to date totals 64 actions, reflecting fewer and larger-value awards on average based on the reported average award size. This profile focuses on contract obligations rather than total contract values, and current-year totals for Huntington Ingalls are partial because the fiscal year is still in progress.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Huntington Ingalls' federal business changed recently?",
        "body": "Huntington Ingalls' obligations fell 29.9% year over year to $2.9B in FY2026 to date. Huntington Ingalls had higher obligations in FY25 at $4.2B and has seen a multi-year range from $3B to $4.2B before the current-year drop. Huntington Ingalls' current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is still in progress."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where do Huntington Ingalls' obligations concentrate?",
        "body": "Ship Building and Repairing is the largest industry for Huntington Ingalls with $2.8B in FY2026 to date. Huntington Ingalls also shows $58.4M in Engineering Services and $39.6M in Other Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance, with smaller amounts in Power Boiler and Heat Exchanger Manufacturing and Hardware Manufacturing. Huntington Ingalls' award count of 64 and average award size of $45.9M reflect concentration in large shipbuilding awards."
      }
